The attached image illustrates Nano-11's ability to facilitate antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A presents flow cytometry data, showing that Nano-11 significantly increases the percentage of ovalbumin (OVA)-containing cells and their mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) in lymph nodes compared to soluble OVA or aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. Panel B quantifies the higher OVA MFI in cells with Nano-11, indicating more efficient antigen delivery per cell. Panel C reveals that Nano-11 preferentially targets migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) with OVA, enhancing the subsequent immune response.